  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Define an operation \\(*\\) for positive real numbers by \\(a*b=\\dfrac{ab}{a+b}.\\) Then \\(4*(4*4)\\) equals:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac34\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac43\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{16}{3}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "4/3"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1968-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "First, \\(4*4=\\frac{16}{8}=2.\\) Therefore \\(4*(4*4)=4*2,\\) which equals \\(\\frac{8}{4+2}=\\frac{4}{3}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Evaluate the inner operation first",
        "After finding \\(4*4,\\) substitute it as the second input"
      ],
